href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-menu"><summary role="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-controls="site-navigation"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav id="site-navigation" class="site-nav site-nav--mobile" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></details></div></header><div class="library-nav" aria-label="Library sections" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell library-nav__inner" data-v-e230b581><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Workflows</a><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Agents</a><a href="/library/orchestrators/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Orchestrators</a><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Integrations</a><a aria-current="page" href="/library/articles/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-e230b581>Articles</a></div></div><main id="main" class="library-main" data-v-e230b581><nav class="library-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-v-e230b581 data-v-59391fa3><div class="shell" data-v-59391fa3><ol data-v-59391fa3><!--[--><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Home</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Library</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a aria-current="page" href="/library/articles/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-59391fa3>Articles</a></li><!--]--></ol></div></nav><!--[--><section class="catalog-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="library-kicker">StackOS Library / Articles</p><h1>Practical answers with <em>the work attached.</em></h1><p class="catalog-hero__lede">Direct explanations, field-tested methods, and source-backed examples for people building a dependable way to work with AI.</p><div class="catalog-hero__meta"><span>20 guides</span><span>Firsthand practice and primary sources</span><span>Reviewed for claims, voice, and disclosure</span></div></div></section><section class="library-section"><div class="shell article-grid"><!--[--><a href="/library/articles/building-ai-finance-department-one-person-business/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>Building an AI finance department for a one-person business</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>A practical design for AI-supported finance operations in a one-person business, with clear authority, verification, and escalation boundaries.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/customer-paid-invoice-still-open/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>4 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>A customer paid. Why is the invoice still open?</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>A proposed payment-follow-up agent can match received money, preserve an open balance, and choose the next contact decision for a solo entrepreneur.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/managing-a-solo-agency-with-ai-agents/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>Managing a solo agency with AI agents</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>A proposed way to organize a solo agency with AI agents, keeping engagement work, cross-project commitments, and company finance in clear working contexts.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/when-is-a-receipt-actually-processed/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>3 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>When is a receipt actually processed?</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>A proposed receipt agent can separate readable documents, preserve unresolved attachments, and prepare a clear handoff for a solo entrepreneur.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-separate-issue-investigation-from-implementation/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How to separate issue investigation from implementation</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Turn a software issue report into a supported conclusion, an authorized change, and acceptance checks. Follow a worked CSV export example.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-ai-agents-should-explain-blockers-to-humans/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>3 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How an AI agent can explain a blocker without assigning the repair</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Use a short blocker message to explain the waiting action, ask for help within the recipient&#39;s authority, and show what the agent must check before continuing.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-build-ai-content-workflow-that-does-not-sound-generic/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--roles is-compact" style="--visual-color:#7892ff;" role="img" aria-label="Focused agents. One complete job. AI operations. A team around the work." data-v-b4c14f53 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>A team around the work</span><strong data-v-9361e887>Focused agents. One complete job.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Agent teamwork</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Chooses the right role</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Specialists</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Research</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Create</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Review</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>Why an AI content workflow can still sound generic</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Find why an AI-written draft feels generic. Use concrete examples to trace the problem to missing evidence, a vague brief, repeated structure, or wording.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-do-keyword-research-for-ai-search/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>7 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How to do keyword research for AI search</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>A case-led research method for deciding what a natural-language AI-search question can support when conventional keyword fields are missing.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-use-product-evidence-without-writing-a-product-pitch/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>4 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How to use product evidence without writing a product pitch</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Choose product details that help a reader judge a claim. Work through a real connection-flow example, its test scope, and the decision it supports.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-fact-check-ai-generated-content/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI content</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>5 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>Fact-check AI-generated content one claim at a time</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Check an AI-written claim against its source, work through a hypothetical example, and decide what to keep, qualify, remove, or send for specialist review.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/ai-workflow-automation/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>5 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>AI workflow automation: automate the rules, not the judgment</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Decide which workflow checks belong in code, which need an agent to interpret evidence, and when a person must supply missing intent or permission.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-ai-orchestrators-triage-feedback/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How should an AI orchestrator triage feedback?</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Work through a mixed review queue to decide which findings need a repair, who should make it, and what to check before calling the work complete.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-refine-ai-agent-workflow/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--workflow is-compact" style="--visual-color:#d9ff63;" role="img" aria-label="A complete plan you can follow. AI operations. From request to result." data-v-b4c14f53 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>From request to result</span><strong data-v-9361e887>A complete plan you can follow.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Visible plan</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Builds the plan</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Visible stages</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Plan</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Do</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Check</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>8 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How to refine an AI agent workflow: best practices after the first working version</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Refine a working AI agent workflow with fresh agent trials, post-run debriefs, trace checks, and bounded repairs. Includes a prompt and questions to use.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/what-ai-agent-handoff-should-include/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--workflow is-compact" style="--visual-color:#d9ff63;" role="img" aria-label="A complete plan you can follow. AI operations. From request to result." data-v-b4c14f53 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>From request to result</span><strong data-v-9361e887>A complete plan you can follow.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Visible plan</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Builds the plan</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Visible stages</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Plan</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Do</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Check</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>9 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>What should an AI agent handoff include?</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Build an AI agent handoff with the objective, evidence, context, tools, expected result, and stopping rule. See how to continue after an interrupted update.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/ai-agent-experience/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>Agent experience: the missing layer in AI agent orchestration</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Turn a vague review request into an assignment an agent can carry out. See how exact inputs, authority, evidence, recovery, and a stopping rule fit together.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-to-build-ai-agent-workflow/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>7 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How to build an AI agent workflow: start with the problem</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Design an AI agent workflow around a useful result. Follow one article-preparation example through inputs, dependencies, review, recovery, and a clear stopping point.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/ai-agent-vs-workflow-vs-orchestrator/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--roles is-compact" style="--visual-color:#7892ff;" role="img" aria-label="Focused agents. One complete job. AI operations. A team around the work." data-v-b4c14f53 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>A team around the work</span><strong data-v-9361e887>Focused agents. One complete job.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Agent teamwork</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Chooses the right role</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Specialists</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Research</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Create</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Review</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>AI operations</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>8 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>AI agent vs. workflow vs. orchestrator: what is the difference?</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>A workflow stores the execution contract. Agents own bounded responsibilities. The orchestrator reasons about the whole job and gates feedback, exceptions, and drift.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/how-ai-agents-use-accounts-safely/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><!----><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>Security</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>6 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How can AI agents use business accounts without seeing the login?</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>See how StackOS keeps credentials in its runtime, checks a Search Console action against separate permissions, and distinguishes three ways to remove account access.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/use-codex-claude-gemini-with-existing-tools/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--connections is-compact" style="--visual-color:#79dfff;" role="img" aria-label="Your AI works across your apps. Getting started. Keep the tools you use." data-v-b4c14f53 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>Keep the tools you use</span><strong data-v-9361e887>Your AI works across your apps.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Connected work</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Connects the plan</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Connected apps</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Slack</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Shopify</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> WordPress</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>Getting started</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>5 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>How to use Codex, Claude Code, or Gemini CLI with the tools you already have</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>Keep your preferred AI client and existing business apps. Connect each client to the same durable project so plans, tool access, credentials, and receipts do not disappear with the chat.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><a href="/library/articles/what-is-an-agentic-workflow/" class="article-card" data-v-b4c14f53><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--workflow is-compact" style="--visual-color:#d9ff63;" role="img" aria-label="A complete plan you can follow. Agentic workflows. From request to result." data-v-b4c14f53 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>From request to result</span><strong data-v-9361e887>A complete plan you can follow.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Visible plan</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Builds the plan</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Visible stages</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Plan</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Do</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Check</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="article-card__meta" data-v-b4c14f53><span data-v-b4c14f53>Agentic workflows</span><span data-v-b4c14f53>8 min read</span></div><h3 data-v-b4c14f53>What is an agentic workflow? A practical guide to AI-powered work</h3><p data-v-b4c14f53>An agentic workflow lets AI choose its next action from the evidence. Follow a content example through source checks, decisions, review, recovery, and a finished draft.</p><b data-v-b4c14f53>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-b4c14f53>→</span></b></a><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></main><footer class="site-footer" data-v-e230b581 data-v-5f58f905><div class="shell site-footer__grid" data-v-5f58f905><a href="/" class="footer-brand" data-v-5f58f905><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width